{"id": "q0328", "pool": "easy-fact", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, let's start with the year 1 90 9. That was a big year for Wassily K andinsky because he moved to Munich in Germany to study art at the Academy of Fine Arts. It was there that he really started developing his unique style by combining color s and shapes in interesting ways. He also met other artists like Franz Marc who would later become one of his closest friends and collaborators. In 1 9 11, he published an essay called \"On the Spiritual in Art\" which laid out his belief that abstract painting could express deep emotions without needing to show realistic images. Then in 1912, he co-founded the group Der Blaue Re if or The Blue R iff with some other artist s. They wanted to explore new forms of expression through abstract art. By 19 1 3, Kand insky had already created many abstract works like Composition VII which shows dynamic swirl s and bold colors reflecting his inner feelings. Later on during World War I, he served in the army but continued to paint when he could. After the war, he became more experimental with different media including drawing s and watercol ors. Throughout the", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
